WHAT GETS REFUSED: entries that lean one way, or run in order.
NOTHING IS LOST: what you entered is kept. keep going.␀␀WHY YOU DO THIS BY HAND␀you roll a die 50 times.␀␀␀␀PATTERN␀these run in order. chance does not.␀␀␀␀your seed words come only from these rolls.␀ROLL A DIE␀␀UNDO␀␀␀␀UNEVEN␀␀some faces came up far more than the rest␀␀␀your rolls, then SHA256. check on any computer.␀a key someone can guess␀nothing lost, keep going␀␀␀␀THE FIX␀CHECK WHAT YOU ENTERED␀␀ADD YOUR TAPS␀␀␀source 1 done.␀␀the sources did not combine, so nothing was saved. you had no keys yet, so nothing was lost.␀␀␀␀NO SEED WORDS MADE␀␀good. keep it there.␀␀␀␀too dark or too plain. point somewhere busier.␀␀WHAT YOU POINT AT: the scene in front of the lens.
THE CHIP ITSELF: hardware noise, on since boot.
YOUR OWN HANDS: the exact moment of each tap.
THE TIMING INSIDE: tiny delays as this board works.
